IMPORT prelude

-- Water Services Act 2012 (Western Australia), Part 5 -- water service charges, from the seat of the property owner: who
-- may charge me for water services to my home, whether I am entitled to the service, who is liable for the charges (owner
-- or tenant), how unpaid charges follow the land, what happens if I pay late, when my supply may be cut off or reduced,
-- and what the Act gives me on hardship, concessions and disputes.
--
-- SEAT: the property owner -- the owner of land to which a licensee (in practice the water utility) provides a water
-- supply, sewerage or drainage service ("What water charges apply to my home?"). Every exported question is phrased as
-- that owner would ask it. What the Act tells the licensee, the Authority or the Registrar to do is encoded only as what
-- it means for the owner: what may be charged, what may be done to the supply or the title, and what the owner must be
-- given.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED: s 3(1) (customer, dwelling, owner, occupier -- owner and occupier borrowed from the Local Government
-- Act 1995 s 1.4 and asked as FACTS); s 21(1)(a), (2) (duty to provide the service; refusal or suspension); s 27(3)(e), (4)
-- (the code of conduct on financial hardship, as a pointer); ss 65(1), 66(2)(g), 68(1), 69(2) (the water services
-- ombudsman); s 71(1) (water service charge, statutory water service charge, quality/quantity charge); s 73 (the owner's
-- statutory entitlement to the service); s 75(2), (3) (agreements and alternative charges); s 76(3), (4), (6), (7)
-- (agreements binding a later owner); s 77(1)-(3) (interruption, and when the licensee is liable for loss); s 79(1), (2)
-- (meters presumed accurate); s 95(1)-(3), (6), (7) (cutting off or reducing the supply; the occupied dwelling; restoring
-- the supply); s 123 (licensees may impose fees and charges); s 124(2)(c), (d), (n), (o) (what the regulations may do:
-- unconnected land, user liability, late payment, exemptions); s 125 (groups of dwellings on one connection); s 126(1)
-- (charges payable despite a change of ownership); s 128(2)-(4) (memorial against dealings in the land); s 129(2), (4), (5)
-- (meter reading and routine inspection); s 222(2)(c) (exemptions, discounts, rebates and concessions by regulation).
--
-- Edition: the Water Services Act 2012 (No. 24 of 2012) as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_48881.txt
-- (legislation.wa.gov.au mrdoc 48881, retrieved 2026-09-07); the compilation table runs to the Statutes (Repeals and Minor
-- Amendments) Act 2025 s 8 (in operation 26 Sep 2025). No regulations, code of practice or code of conduct under the Act
-- is deposited. The tariffs (the statutory water service charges themselves), the interest and late-payment penalties
-- (s 124(2)(n)), the exemptions and concessions (ss 124(2)(o), 222(2)(c)), the prescribed restoration fees (s 95(7)) and
-- the hardship rules of the code of conduct (s 27(3)(e)) are therefore INPUTS or pointers, and are said to be so where used.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: Part 2 except ss 21 and 27 (licensing); Part 3 (last resort supply); Part 4 beyond the right to apply to the
-- ombudsman; Part 5 Divisions 3, 4, 6, 7 and 8 (development control and infrastructure contributions, protection of
-- works, sewer and drainage connections, enforcement) except as s 128 refers to them; s 127 (unlawful takers); Parts 6-11
-- (works, interests in land, entry beyond s 129, proceedings, administration, miscellaneous); the trade-waste rules. Council
-- rates, the emergency services levy and land tax, which the same life event cites, are other Acts.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill from the seat of the property owner, with the design defaults
-- ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice.
-- See NOTES.md.
--
-- Conventions. Money is in dollars. Periods are counted in whole days.

§ `Water Services Act 2012 -- the property owner`

§§ `s 123 -- who may charge me, and for what?`

-- s 123(1): "A licensee may impose and collect, in relation to the provision of a water service authorised by a licence --
-- (a) charges for the provision of the service; and (b) charges for things done, or goods and services provided, as part
-- of or incidental to the provision of the service; and (c) fees, provided for in the regulations, for things done under
-- this Act."
-- (2): "The charges are to be determined by the licensee in accordance with prudent commercial principles and may allow for
-- the making of a profit and the depreciation of assets."
-- (3): conditions on the licence, a code of practice or the regulations may limit the charges.
-- "licensee" (s 3(1)): "the holder of a licence" -- the water utility that provides the service.
DECLARE `What I am being asked to pay` IS ONE OF
    `a charge for the water service itself`
    `a charge for something done or supplied as part of, or incidental to, the service`
    `a fee provided for in the regulations for something done under the Act`
    `something with no basis in s 123`

@export Who may charge me for water services to my home, and on what footing (s 123)?
GIVEN `the item` IS A `What I am being asked to pay` @desc What the item on your bill is for
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `Who may charge me for this` IS
    CONSIDER `the item`
    WHEN `a charge for the water service itself` THEN
        "the licensee providing the service, set on prudent commercial principles (which may include a profit), subject to any limit in its licence, a code of practice or the regulations (s 123(1)(a), (2), (3))"
    WHEN `a charge for something done or supplied as part of, or incidental to, the service` THEN
        "the licensee providing the service, set on prudent commercial principles, subject to any limit in its licence, a code of practice or the regulations (s 123(1)(b), (2), (3))"
    WHEN `a fee provided for in the regulations for something done under the Act` THEN
        "the licensee, but only in the amount the regulations provide for (s 123(1)(c))"
    OTHERWISE
        "no one under s 123: a licensee's power to charge is limited to the three heads in s 123(1)"

§§ `s 73 -- am I entitled to the service?`

-- s 73(1): "The owner of land in respect of which statutory water service charges apply for the provision of a water
-- service by a licensee is entitled to the provision of the water service." (2): "The owner's entitlement is subject to --
-- (a) the terms and conditions of the provision of the service; and (b) the charges referred to in subsection (1), that are
-- due to the licensee, being paid; and (c) the provisions of this Part."
-- "statutory water service charge" (s 71(1)): "a water service charge payable under the regulations".
-- "owner" (s 3(1)): "an owner of the land within the meaning given in the Local Government Act 1995 section 1.4" -- a FACT
-- here; s 71(2)(b) includes the owner of a strata or community titles lot.
@export Am I, as owner, entitled to have the water service provided to my land (s 73)?
GIVEN `I am the owner of the land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an owner of the land (Local Government Act 1995 s 1.4), including the owner of a strata or community titles lot
      `statutory charges apply to my land for the service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether charges under the regulations apply to your land for this service (water supply, sewerage or drainage)
      `the charges due have been paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the charges for the service that are already due to the licensee have been paid
      `I am keeping to the terms and conditions of the service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are complying with the terms and conditions of the service (the licensee's standard terms, or your agreement)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to the water service` IF
        `I am the owner of the land`
    AND `statutory charges apply to my land for the service`
    AND `the charges due have been paid`
    AND `I am keeping to the terms and conditions of the service`

-- s 124(2)(c): the regulations may "provide that specified statutory water service charges apply in respect of land
-- despite relevant water service works not being connected to an inlet or outlet on land if -- (i) it is practicable for
-- an inlet or outlet on the land to be connected to those works (which includes that the works run within, at or near a
-- boundary of the land); or (ii) the land benefits from the service; or (iii) the land contributes to the need for the
-- service". Whether the regulations do so for a given charge is an INPUT (not deposited).
@export Can I be charged for a water service my land is not yet connected to (s 124(2)(c))?
GIVEN `the regulations apply this charge to unconnected land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations (not deposited) say this charge applies to land not connected to the works
      `connection is practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is practicable to connect your land, for example because the main runs within, at or near your boundary
      `my land benefits from the service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your land benefits from the service
      `my land contributes to the need for the service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your land contributes to the need for the service
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be charged for a service I am not connected to` IF
        `the regulations apply this charge to unconnected land`
    AND (    `connection is practicable`
          OR `my land benefits from the service`
          OR `my land contributes to the need for the service`)

§§ `ss 124, 125, 126 -- who is liable for the charges: owner or tenant?`

-- s 126(1): "Despite any change in the ownership of land, statutory water service charges and alternative water service
-- charges (referred to in section 75(2)(c)), including interest on overdue amounts, remain payable and are recoverable from
-- the owner of the land for the time being while the charges remain unpaid."
-- s 124(2)(d): the regulations may "provide that a person who is not otherwise liable to pay a specified statutory water
-- service charge is liable to pay the charge, to the extent specified, if the extent to which the person has used the
-- service is measured or can be determined".
-- s 125(1): where 2 or more dwellings are served "by a single property connection, the licensee may apportion the fees and
-- charges for the service (including quality/quantity charges) between the owners or occupiers of the dwellings, and the
-- owners or occupiers become liable to those fees and charges accordingly" -- unless an agreement, the Community Titles Act
-- 2018 s 64 or the Strata Titles Act 1985 s 75 is inconsistent (s 125(2)).
-- The Act itself never makes a tenant as such liable; it lets the regulations make a user liable for measured use, and
-- lets the licensee apportion among occupiers on a shared connection. Both are asked as FACTS.
DECLARE `Kind of charge` IS ONE OF
    `a statutory water service charge`
    `an alternative charge under an agreement in place of a statutory charge`
    `a charge under an agreement where no statutory charge applies`
    `a charge for something incidental to the service`

GIVEN `the charge` IS A `Kind of charge`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 126 reaches this charge` IF
    CONSIDER `the charge`
    WHEN `a statutory water service charge` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an alternative charge under an agreement in place of a statutory charge` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

@export Can the unpaid water charges on this land be recovered from me as its owner, even if they arose before I owned it (s 126(1))?
GIVEN `the charge` IS A `Kind of charge` @desc What kind of charge it is: statutory (under the regulations), an alternative charge in an agreement replacing a statutory one, a charge under an agreement where no statutory charge applies, or an incidental charge
      `I am the owner for the time being` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are now an owner of the land (Local Government Act 1995 s 1.4)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the unpaid charges on my land be recovered from me as owner` IF
    `I am the owner for the time being` AND `s 126 reaches this charge` `the charge`

DECLARE `Who the Act makes liable` IS ONE OF
    `the owner only`
    `the owner, and the tenant to the extent the regulations make a measured user liable`
    `each owner or occupier for the share the licensee apportioned`

@export Who is liable for the water charges on my home: me as owner, or my tenant (ss 124(2)(d), 125, 126(1))?
GIVEN `the regulations make the tenant liable for measured use` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations (not deposited) make a person who is not otherwise liable, such as a tenant, liable for a charge because their use is measured
      `the licensee has apportioned the charges between dwellings on one connection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your home is one of 2 or more dwellings on a single property connection and the licensee has apportioned the charges between their owners or occupiers (s 125)
GIVETH A `Who the Act makes liable`
DECIDE `Who is liable for the water charges on my home` IS
    IF `the licensee has apportioned the charges between dwellings on one connection`
    THEN `each owner or occupier for the share the licensee apportioned`
    ELSE IF `the regulations make the tenant liable for measured use`
         THEN `the owner, and the tenant to the extent the regulations make a measured user liable`
         ELSE `the owner only`

-- s 126(1) keeps statutory charges recoverable from "the owner of the land for the time being while the charges remain
-- unpaid", whoever else may also be liable. INFERENCE (labelled): a tenant's liability under regulations does not release
-- the owner.
@export If my tenant is also liable but does not pay, can the statutory charges still be recovered from me (s 126(1))?
GIVEN `I am the owner for the time being` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are now an owner of the land
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the charges still be recovered from me if my tenant does not pay` IF `I am the owner for the time being`

§§ `s 76 -- am I bound by the previous owner's agreement?`

-- s 76(3): "Unless the agreement provides otherwise, the terms and conditions of the agreement are binding on each
-- subsequent owner of the land who has prior notice of the agreement". (4): terms "relating to -- (a) any aspects of the
-- service that do not ordinarily apply to a service of that type; or (b) the quantity or quality of water supplied or
-- wastewater discharged; or (c) water service charges; or (d) the indemnification of the licensee ..., are binding on
-- each subsequent owner of the land whether or not the owner has prior notice". (6), (7): prior notice is taken if a
-- notification is registered (or the title endorsed) "at least 21 days before the day on which the subsequent owner became
-- the owner", that is, obtained possession. Both bindings last "until the service is no longer required or the subsequent
-- owner enters into an agreement about the service". Actual notice by other means is a FACT.
DECLARE `Term of the earlier agreement` IS ONE OF
    `a term about water service charges`
    `a term about an unusual aspect of the service`
    `a term about the quantity or quality of water or wastewater`
    `a term indemnifying the licensee`
    `any other term`

@export Am I, as a later owner, bound by a term of an agreement the previous owner made with the licensee (s 76)?
GIVEN `the term` IS A `Term of the earlier agreement` @desc What the term of the earlier written agreement is about
      `days before I took possession that a notification was registered` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days before you obtained possession a notification of the agreement was registered or endorsed on the title (0 if none)
      `I otherwise had prior notice of the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you knew of the agreement before you became owner, apart from registration
      `the agreement says it does not bind later owners` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agreement itself provides that it does not bind later owners
      `I have made my own agreement about the service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have since entered into your own agreement with the licensee about the service, or the service is no longer required
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I bound by the previous owner's agreement` IF
        (NOT `the agreement says it does not bind later owners`)
    AND (NOT `I have made my own agreement about the service`)
    AND (    `the term binds whatever my notice`
          OR `I had prior notice`)
    WHERE
        `the term binds whatever my notice` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the term`
            WHEN `any other term` THEN FALSE
            OTHERWISE TRUE
        `I had prior notice` MEANS
               `days before I took possession that a notification was registered` AT LEAST 21
            OR `I otherwise had prior notice of the agreement`

§§ `s 128 -- can unpaid charges stop me dealing with my land?`

-- s 128(2): if "(a) a statutory water service charge, or an alternative water service charge, that applies in respect of
-- land is in arrears; or (b) an infrastructure contribution has been deferred ... or is in arrears; or (c) the reasonable
-- cost and expenses of a licensee referred to in section 84(5) or 121(6) is in arrears, the licensee may lodge a memorial
-- to that effect with the Registrar". (3): "Until the memorial is withdrawn, the Registrar must not register, without the
-- written consent of the licensee, an instrument affecting the land that is lodged for registration after the memorial is
-- lodged." (4): "If the charge or contribution has been paid, the licensee must lodge a withdrawal of memorial".
-- The Act does not call unpaid charges "a charge on the land" in those words; the memorial and s 126(1) do that work.
DECLARE `What is unpaid` IS ONE OF
    `statutory or alternative water service charges in arrears`
    `an infrastructure contribution deferred or in arrears`
    `the licensee's costs of remedying a failure, in arrears`
    `nothing, or something else`

@export Can the licensee lodge a memorial on my title for what I owe (s 128(2))?
GIVEN `what is unpaid` IS A `What is unpaid` @desc What, if anything, is unpaid on the land
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the licensee lodge a memorial on my title` IF
    CONSIDER `what is unpaid`
    WHEN `nothing, or something else` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

@export Can a sale, mortgage or other dealing with my land be registered while a water memorial stands (s 128(3))?
GIVEN `a memorial has been lodged and not withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the licensee has lodged a memorial against the land that has not been withdrawn
      `my instrument was lodged after the memorial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the transfer, mortgage or other instrument was lodged for registration after the memorial
      `the licensee has consented in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the licensee has given its written consent to registration
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my dealing be registered despite a memorial` IF
       (NOT `a memorial has been lodged and not withdrawn`)
    OR (NOT `my instrument was lodged after the memorial`)
    OR `the licensee has consented in writing`

@export Once I have paid, must the licensee withdraw the memorial (s 128(4))?
GIVEN `the charge or contribution has been paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the arrears the memorial was lodged for have been paid
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the licensee withdraw the memorial` IF `the charge or contribution has been paid`

§§ `s 124(2)(n) -- what do I owe if I pay late?`

-- s 124(2)(n): the regulations may "provide for penalties for late payment or underpayment of charges, interest to be
-- payable on overdue charges and for the recovery of overdue amounts". s 126(1) and s 95 speak of "interest on overdue
-- amounts" as part of the charges. The rates and methods are in the regulations (not deposited): the interest and any
-- late-payment penalty are INPUTS, as amounts.
@export How much do I owe on an overdue water bill (s 124(2)(n))?
GIVEN `the unpaid charges` IS A NUMBER @desc The water service charges still unpaid, in dollars
      `interest on the overdue amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The interest the regulations charge on the overdue amount, in dollars (0 if none)
      `late payment penalty` IS A NUMBER @desc Any penalty the regulations impose for late payment, in dollars (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much do I owe on an overdue bill` IS
    `the unpaid charges` PLUS `interest on the overdue amount` PLUS `late payment penalty`

§§ `s 95 -- can my water be cut off or reduced?`

-- s 95(1): "A licensee may cut off, reduce the rate of flow of or refuse to connect a supply of water to land if -- (a) the
-- land is unoccupied; or (b) water service charges (including interest on overdue amounts) due to the licensee for a
-- water service provided in respect of the land remain unpaid for 30 days after they become due; or (c) the occupier (or
-- the owner if there is no occupier) of the land refuses to permit a meter to be installed ...; or (d) the owner of the
-- land requests that the licensee do so; or (e) another provision of this Act authorises the licensee to do so."
-- (2): "A licensee may reduce the rate of flow ... if satisfied that it is necessary to do so to prevent the waste of
-- water" -- the licensee's judgment, asked as a FACT and answered conditionally.
-- (3): "Despite any other provision of this Act, a licensee cannot cut off the supply of water to an occupied dwelling
-- unless the occupier agrees to that."
-- (4): subject to any restriction in the licence's terms and conditions (a FACT).
-- "dwelling" (s 3(1)): a building or part "ordinarily used for human habitation ... (whether or not it is uninhabited from
-- time to time)", or a mobile home. "remain unpaid for 30 days after they become due": read here as at least 30 days
-- elapsed since the due date.
DECLARE `What may be done to my supply` IS ONE OF
    `it may be cut off or its flow reduced`
    `its flow may be reduced, but it cannot be cut off without the occupier's agreement`
    `its flow may be reduced, if the licensee is satisfied that is necessary to prevent waste`
    `neither`

@export Can my water supply be cut off or reduced (s 95(1)-(4))?
GIVEN `days the charges have been unpaid since falling due` IS A NUMBER @desc Days since the due date that water service charges (with interest) have remained unpaid (0 if nothing is overdue)
      `the land is unoccupied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the land is unoccupied
      `a meter installation has been refused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the occupier (or the owner, if no occupier) has refused to let a meter be installed
      `the owner has asked for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the owner has asked the licensee to cut off or reduce the supply
      `the licensee is satisfied a reduction is needed to prevent waste` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the licensee is satisfied a reduction in flow is necessary to prevent the waste of water on the land
      `there is an occupied dwelling on the land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the supply goes to a dwelling that is occupied
      `the occupier agrees to being cut off` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the occupier has agreed to the supply being cut off
      `the licence forbids it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the terms and conditions of the licensee's licence restrict cutting off or reducing in this case
GIVETH A `What may be done to my supply`
DECIDE `Can my water be cut off or reduced` IS
    IF `the licence forbids it` THEN `neither`
    ELSE IF `a s 95(1) ground exists`
         THEN IF `there is an occupied dwelling on the land` AND (NOT `the occupier agrees to being cut off`)
              THEN `its flow may be reduced, but it cannot be cut off without the occupier's agreement`
              ELSE `it may be cut off or its flow reduced`
         ELSE IF `the licensee is satisfied a reduction is needed to prevent waste`
              THEN `its flow may be reduced, if the licensee is satisfied that is necessary to prevent waste`
              ELSE `neither`
    WHERE
        `a s 95(1) ground exists` MEANS
               `the land is unoccupied`
            OR `days the charges have been unpaid since falling due` AT LEAST 30
            OR `a meter installation has been refused`
            OR `the owner has asked for it`

-- s 95(6): cutting off or reducing "does not prevent -- (a) the licensee from taking action to recover unpaid charges
-- (including interest on overdue amounts)".
@export If my water is cut off or reduced, does that end what I owe (s 95(6))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does being cut off end what I owe` IS FALSE

-- s 95(7): before restoring, the licensee may "(a) require payment of unpaid water service charges (including interest on
-- overdue amounts) and any prescribed fees in relation to cutting off or reducing ... or restoring ...; or (b) require
-- arrangements satisfactory to the licensee to be made for the payment". The fees are prescribed (not deposited): INPUTS.
-- Whether an arrangement is satisfactory is the licensee's judgment: asked as a FACT.
@export What can I be required to pay before my water is restored (s 95(7))?
GIVEN `the unpaid charges with interest` IS A NUMBER @desc The unpaid water service charges, with interest on overdue amounts, in dollars
      `the prescribed disconnection and restoration fees` IS A NUMBER @desc The prescribed fees for cutting off or reducing and for restoring the supply (regulations not deposited), in dollars
      `the licensee has accepted a payment arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have made arrangements for payment that the licensee is satisfied with
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What must I pay before my water is restored` IS
    IF `the licensee has accepted a payment arrangement`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the unpaid charges with interest` PLUS `the prescribed disconnection and restoration fees`

§§ `s 77 -- interruptions`

-- s 77(1): the licensee "may interrupt, suspend or restrict the provision of a water service to the extent to which it is
-- necessary, in the licensee's opinion, ... because of an accident, emergency, potential danger or other unavoidable cause,
-- or for the purposes of maintenance and repair". (2): the licensee "is not liable for any loss or damage that arises ...
-- except to the extent to which -- (a) the interruption ... results from -- (i) a negligent act or omission of the licensee;
-- or (ii) an act or omission of the licensee done or made in bad faith; or (b) the licensee has agreed otherwise."
-- Negligence and bad faith are borrowed (general law) and asked as FACTS.
@export Can I claim from the licensee for loss caused by an interruption to my water service (s 77(2))?
GIVEN `it resulted from the licensee's negligence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the interruption resulted from a negligent act or omission of the licensee
      `it resulted from the licensee's bad faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the interruption resulted from an act or omission of the licensee in bad faith
      `the licensee agreed to be liable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the licensee has agreed to be liable for such loss
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I claim for loss from an interruption` IF
       `it resulted from the licensee's negligence`
    OR `it resulted from the licensee's bad faith`
    OR `the licensee agreed to be liable`

§§ `s 79 -- my meter`

-- s 79(1): "For all purposes, a meter is to be presumed to be operating within the prescribed tolerance for that type of
-- meter unless there is evidence to the contrary." (2): a certificate of readings signed for the licensee "is to be
-- presumed to correctly set out those matters unless there is evidence to the contrary". Testing rights are for the
-- regulations (s 79(3); not deposited).
@export Is my meter, and the licensee's certificate of its readings, presumed correct (s 79(1), (2))?
GIVEN `there is evidence the meter or reading is wrong` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is evidence that the meter is outside tolerance or the reading is wrong
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my meter presumed correct` IF (NOT `there is evidence the meter or reading is wrong`)

-- s 129(2): a person authorised by the licensee "may enter, at all reasonable times, a place without consent, notice or
-- warrant for the purpose of reading a meter". (4): that power extends "to the area associated with a dwelling but not to
-- the dwelling itself". (5): "If routine inspection or maintenance is likely to cause disruption to the occupants of a place,
-- at least 48 hours' notice of the proposed entry is required to be given to the occupier ..., unless the occupier agrees
-- otherwise."
DECLARE `Why they want to come in` IS ONE OF
    `to read the meter`
    `for routine inspection or maintenance`

@export How many hours' notice must I be given before the licensee's people come onto my land (s 129(2), (5))?
GIVEN `the purpose` IS A `Why they want to come in` @desc Why the licensee's authorised person wants to enter
      `it is likely to disrupt the occupants` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the routine inspection or maintenance is likely to cause disruption to the occupants
      `the occupier agreed to less notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the occupier has agreed otherwise
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many hours notice must I get before entry` IS
    CONSIDER `the purpose`
    WHEN `to read the meter` THEN 0
    WHEN `for routine inspection or maintenance` THEN
        IF `it is likely to disrupt the occupants` AND (NOT `the occupier agreed to less notice`)
        THEN 48
        ELSE 0

§§ `ss 27, 124(2)(o), 222(2)(c) -- hardship and concessions`

-- s 27(3): the Authority's code of conduct "may deal with ... (e) the provision of water services to customers in financial
-- hardship; (f) the suspension of the provision of water services". (4): "It is a condition of every licence that the
-- licensee must comply with the code of conduct". The code is not deposited, so the Act gives the owner only this pointer.
@export What does the Act give me if I am in financial hardship and cannot pay my water charges (s 27(3)(e), (4))?
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `What does the Act give me in financial hardship` IS
    "no hardship rule of its own: the Economic Regulation Authority's code of conduct may deal with customers in financial hardship and with suspension of services, and every licensee must comply with it as a licence condition (s 27(3)(e), (f), (4)); the code is not deposited here. Separately, the supply to an occupied dwelling cannot be cut off without the occupier's agreement (s 95(3))."

-- s 124(2)(o): the regulations may "provide for land to be exempt from water service charges". s 222(2)(c): the regulations
-- may, "in respect of fees and charges, deal with exemptions, discounts, rebates and concessions to be made available to
-- customers". None is deposited: whether the regulations give one is an INPUT. Concessions under other Acts are not read.
DECLARE `What the regulations give me` IS ONE OF
    `an exemption`
    `a discount, rebate or concession`
    `nothing`

@export Am I entitled to an exemption, discount, rebate or concession on my water charges (ss 124(2)(o), 222(2)(c))?
GIVEN `what the regulations give me` IS A `What the regulations give me` @desc What the regulations (not deposited) make available to you
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `Am I entitled to a concession on my water charges` IS
    CONSIDER `what the regulations give me`
    WHEN `an exemption` THEN "yes: the land is exempt from the charges the regulations specify (s 124(2)(o))"
    WHEN `a discount, rebate or concession` THEN "yes: to the extent the regulations provide (s 222(2)(c))"
    OTHERWISE "not under this Act: the Act itself grants no concession; only the regulations may (ss 124(2)(o), 222(2)(c))"

§§ `ss 68, 69 -- disputes`

-- s 68(1): "The following persons may apply to the water services ombudsman under an approved scheme for a review of a
-- decision or complaint to which the scheme relates -- (a) a customer; (b) a person affected by the provision of a water
-- service by the licensee or a failure by the licensee to provide a water service". s 69(2): the ombudsman "must decline to
-- deal with a matter if -- (a) it has been or is being dealt with by a court or tribunal". s 66(2)(g): the scheme must
-- "operate expeditiously and without cost to complainants".
-- "customer" (s 3(1)): "a person to whom water services are provided by the licensee or who is entitled to the provision of
-- water services by the licensee, other than a person who is a member of the licensee".
@export Can I take my dispute with the water provider to the water services ombudsman, free of charge (ss 3(1), 66(2)(g), 68, 69(2))?
GIVEN `the licensee provides me water services or I am entitled to them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the licensee provides water services to you, or you are entitled to them
      `I am a member of the licensee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a member of the licensee (a cooperative)
      `I am affected by its service or failure to provide one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are affected by the licensee's provision of, or failure to provide, a water service
      `a court or tribunal has dealt with or is dealing with it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court or tribunal has dealt with, or is dealing with, the matter
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I take my dispute to the water ombudsman` IF
        (`I am a customer` OR `I am affected by its service or failure to provide one`)
    AND (NOT `a court or tribunal has dealt with or is dealing with it`)
    WHERE
        `I am a customer` MEANS
            `the licensee provides me water services or I am entitled to them` AND (NOT `I am a member of the licensee`)
